From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: report each XInput request and the slot's answer to
 the host app

0247 has ios_gamepad_query count the game's XInput state requests for
the host app's suggested layout. That count cannot tell why a game
that reads a pad does not react to it: World of Warcraft on the phone
logged its first reads and nothing after, and whether it kept reading,
which slot answered, what it answered and whether the packet number
moved is not in any log.

ios_gamepad_query now reads the slot first and calls the host's
playport_gamepad_query(index, op, connected, packet, buttons) for
every request, state and capability alike, in place of
playport_gamepad_state_read. The host counts state requests as before
(its total feeds the suggested layout unchanged) and a dev build logs
a summary every 10 s while a game asks: reads, from which slots, the
last answer, packet changes and the buttons answered. The reference
stays weak.

Linear: PLA-522
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-01-wow-controller.md (host test app/tests/pads_test.c; phone gate not run)
Offered-upstream: no; the hook feeds the iOS app
---
 build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c | 25 +++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c b/build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c
index 526dfa5..6db315c 100644
--- a/build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c
+++ b/build/win32u-unix/driver_ios.c
@@ -2630,10 +2630,12 @@ C_ASSERT( sizeof(struct ios_xinput_state) == 16 );
 C_ASSERT( sizeof(struct ios_xinput_caps) == 20 );
 C_ASSERT( sizeof(struct winios_gamepad) == 20 );
 
-/* Playport: the host app counts the game's XInput state reads (its
- * HostIO hio_pads.c), to tell a game that never asks for a pad. Weak: a
- * host without it is not called. */
-extern void playport_gamepad_state_read( void ) __attribute__((weak));
+/* Playport: the host app sees each of the game's XInput requests and the
+ * slot's answer (its HostIO hio_pads.c): the count tells a game that never
+ * asks for a pad, and a dev build logs a summary every 10 s. Weak: a host
+ * without it is not called. */
+extern void playport_gamepad_query( unsigned int index, unsigned int op, int connected,
+                                    unsigned int packet, unsigned short buttons ) __attribute__((weak));
 
 /***********************************************************************
  *           ios_gamepad_query
@@ -2648,14 +2650,17 @@ extern void playport_gamepad_state_read( void ) __attribute__((weak));
 ULONG_PTR ios_gamepad_query( UINT index, UINT op, void *buffer )
 {
     struct winios_gamepad pad;
+    int connected;
 
     if (!buffer || index >= 4) return 0;
-    /* Every state request counts (XInputGetState; xinput's SetState and
-     * Enable ask for one too), for a slot with no pad as well: most games ask
-     * all four users each frame. The app's own snapshot reads do not come
-     * here. */
-    if (op == 0 && playport_gamepad_state_read) playport_gamepad_state_read();
-    if (!winios_gamepad_get_state( index, &pad )) return 0;
+    /* Every request is reported (state: XInputGetState; xinput's SetState,
+     * Enable and battery query ask for one too), for a slot with no pad as
+     * well: most games ask all four users each frame. The app's own snapshot
+     * reads do not come here. */
+    connected = winios_gamepad_get_state( index, &pad );
+    if (playport_gamepad_query)
+        playport_gamepad_query( index, op, connected, pad.packet, pad.buttons );
+    if (!connected) return 0;
 
     switch (op)
     {
